# Fullscreen reports clicks to kiln, so the terminal cannot open links;
# kiln opens the link under a click that did not drag. A real terminal's
# mouse encoder sends the click; HARNESS_OPEN_CMD records the URL instead of
# launching a browser. CLICK points are for the 120x40 headless xterm
# (9 px cells after an 8 px left pad, 17.4 px rows): the reply is row 18,
# "PR 45" starts at column 6 and the bare URL at column 59.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/link-click.yaml
@size 120x40
@args --fullscreen
@env HARNESS_OPEN_CMD=printf '%s\n' "$1" >> {HOME}/opened.txt

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE show me the links
KEY enter
WAITFOR /PR 45/ 20
SHOT reply
CLICK 76 322
WAITFOR /opened https:\/\/github\.com\/6cclab\/ynm\/pull\/45/ 5
SHOT opened-markdown-link
CLICK 570 322
WAITFOR /opened https:\/\/example\.com\/x/ 5
SHOT opened-bare-url
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine|open failed/
